  "excerpt": "Courgette and goat's cheese tart is a blind-baked shortcrust case filled with a soft goat's cheese and egg custard, topped with overlapping slices of courgette. The goat's cheese melts into the custard as it bakes, giving a tangy, creamy filling. The courgette on top softens in the oven and takes on a light colour at the edges. This is a savoury tart that serves as a main course with a green salad.",
